description:
In usage-reconcile.js, the snapshot.totals field is replaced with each new reconcile report's totals:

  T.ov.usage_reconcile_snapshot = {
    ...prev,
    totals: report.totals || null,  // ← replaces, not accumulates
  }

When reconcile runs with since=prev.at (incremental), report.totals only contains tokens since the last run. The historical total is discarded. If Claude Code prunes old transcript .jsonl files between reconcile runs, those tokens are permanently lost.

Fix: merge the incremental report.totals INTO the previous snapshot.totals (using mergeTotals), rather than replacing:

  const prevTotals = (prev_snapshot && prev_snapshot.totals) || {};
  const merged = mergeTotals({...prevTotals}, report.totals);
  snapshot.totals = merged;

Also track a separate `since_totals` field for the incremental-only view if needed.

This makes the all-time billing total monotonically increasing and durable against transcript pruning.

